    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'll start with sampling. One thing that's bothering me though is that these aren't just single errors—they seem almost intentional in how they're spread out. Like, they're tiny, annoying amounts that just keep popping up in different places every month. It's hard to pin down a single cause because they're so fragmented. Is there a specific way to look for more \"hidden\" patterns like that? Maybe something more granular than just checking dates?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
